      "html": "<p>This fish comes from Myanmar (former Burma).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/danionella_aff_mirifica_en/",
      "html": "<p>It apparently lives in nature in large formations.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/danionella_aff_mirifica_en/",
      "html": "<p>The adult fish need small food particles, like newly hatched brine shrimps, small copepods and microworms.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/danionella_aff_mirifica_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is a typical shoaling fish. Male fish attract the females for mating with clear croaking noises.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/danionella_aff_mirifica_en/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding is possible in an aquarium with large bushels of plants like Java moss, which give the fry a chance to hide and micro-organisms the opportunity to flourish so they can be used as the first food for the very small fry.</p>"
